course: dictionary
lesson: 4635
title: Hindu: a person or a thing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can name a person and also describe a thing. «Hindu» does both. A Hindu is a person who follows Hinduism, and Hindu describes things linked to Hinduism.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains with lamps, sweets and fireworks.» Hindus is the name of people, so the sentence tells you who celebrates Diwali.
explain: In «Hindu temple» and «Hindu festival», Hindu comes before the thing it describes, so it works as an adjective. Test your meaning by swapping it in: a Hindu temple is a temple to do with Hinduism. It still makes sense.
fact: Hinduism is a major religion that began in India.
fact: A Hindu is a person who follows Hinduism. Hindu can also describe things, such as a Hindu temple, which is called a mandir.
fact: «Hindus believe the soul is reborn in a new body, a person or an animal, until it is freed from the cycle (moksha).»
fact: Hindus see many gods and goddesses, such as Vishnu, Shiva and Ganesh, as forms of one ultimate reality.
fact: Hindus explain their beliefs in different ways, so not every Hindu believes exactly the same thing.
exercise: «Diwali is the festival of lights, celebrated by Hindus, Sikhs and Jains.» Who celebrates Diwali? | *Hindus, Sikhs and Jains | Only the gods | Only children | Only the people who live in the hills
exercise: In «Hindu temple», what kind of word is Hindu? | A verb, because it shows an action | An adverb, because it tells how | *An adjective, because it describes the temple | A noun, because it names a place
exercise: What does mandir mean? | A Hindu god | A Hindu family | A Hindu festival | *A Hindu temple
test: Which word in «Many Hindu families hold prayers and gatherings for about thirteen days after a death» is an adjective? | *Hindu | death | families | prayers
test: Priya says Hindus believe the soul is reborn until it is freed. What do Hindus believe happens to the soul until then? | *It is reborn in a new body, a person or an animal | It becomes a festival | It goes to live in a temple forever | It stops existing at the moment of death
exam: In «Hindus explain it in different ways», what kind of word is Hindus? | *A plural noun naming people | A verb showing an action | An adjective describing a thing | An adverb telling how
